  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Resilience in Border Communities: Climate-Adapted Water Resource Management and Feeder Roads (DARIS WACAN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed action targets border communities in Somalia and Kenya that are impacted by recurrent drought and dependent on transboundary natural resources with insufficient sources of water for human and livestock consumption and agriculture. The objective of this action is to increase these communities&#x2019; access to water for human consumption and agropastoralism, while establishing effective water governance mechanisms for sustainable water resource management. 
 
The International Organization for Migration (IOM) is achieving this through the construction and rehabilitation of ground and surface water infrastructure, complemented by capacity building activities for the border communities on the management and maintenance of the infrastructure. In parallel, the Organization is contributing to social economic development in Somalia through the construction of feeder roads and creation of livelihood opportunities. Finally, IOM aims to improve coordination between government, communities and civil society actors to strengthen cross-border governance. Specific attention is given to building the capacity of border communities and civil society organizations on environmental protection and water conservation.</narrative>
  </description>
